            <creation xml:id="creation_id67796a05">
               <date isodate="1743" xml:id="date_8ad44fbe">1743</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id55f6a0b6">
               <p xml:id="idm62">In 1743, a German translation of six of <persName xml:id="idm63" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Ludvig Holberg</persName>’s comedies was published. The translator was <persName xml:id="idm64" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Johann Georg Laub</persName>. In November a review of the translation appeared in the journal <rend xml:id="idm65" fontstyle="italic">Staats- und Gelehrte Zeitung des Hamburgischen unpartheyischen Correspondenten</rend> and though the reviewer is anonymous it is most likely Scheibe. The review is very critical about the work of Laub listing a whole range of different errors. The translator replied to the critique in <rend xml:id="idm66" fontstyle="italic">Göttingische Zeitungen</rend> already in December that same year.</p>
            </history>
